    "specPath": "specs/035-denials-survive-shutdown/spec.md",
    "status": "draft",
    "summary": "Constitution X says the kernel ledgers every denial. Spec 015 answers a denial before its record is durable and drains the records through a bounded queue, and serve never drains that queue on shutdown, so a graceful stop silently loses the denials still queued (reproduced: 50 denials answered 403 with decision ids, 33 and 40 of them in the chain after SIGTERM, nothing counted). This spec drains the queue within a bound when serve stops, counts what the bound abandons, and separates a dropped record from a failed append on /metrics, so the only uncounted loss left is a process that is killed.\n",
    "title": "Denials survive a graceful shutdown, and every lost denial is counted by its cause"
  },
